---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <main>
    <section class="prd">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="section-tag">
          PRD
        </p>

        <h2>
          LogPulse - AI-powered weekly work summary generator.
        </h2>

        <p class="prd-intro">
          A completed product requirements document for a privacy-first Chrome extension
          that turns GitHub, Jira, and calendar activity into a concise weekly progress report.
        </p>

        <div class="prd-meta">
          <span>Author: Gayatri Gupta</span>
          <span>Status: Completed</span>
          <span>Date: July 24, 2026</span>
          <span>Target Release: NA</span>
        </div>

        <div class="prd-spec">
          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">01 · User Problem</span>
            <p>
              Employees are expected to share weekly progress updates, but remembering
              every contribution across GitHub pull requests, commits, Jira stories,
              meetings, and day-to-day work is difficult. Important work can be missed,
              making it harder to accurately showcase impact.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">02 · AI Value Proposition</span>
            <p>
              LogPulse uses a foundation model to transform raw activity data into a
              concise, human-readable weekly summary. The LLM identifies significant
              contributions, groups related work, and generates structured bullet points
              that employees can quickly review and share.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">03 · Persona & Workflow</span>
            <p>
              Built for software developers and engineering leads. The Chrome extension
              collects weekly activity from connected tools, summarizes the most relevant
              work locally, and presents an editable status update for the user.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">04 · Business Success Metric</span>
            <p>
              Reduce weekly status update preparation from 20-30 minutes of manual
              compilation to approximately 15 seconds of automated summarization.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">05 · Technical Architecture</span>
            <p>
              The model strategy is prompt engineering with a local LLM. Data sources
              include GitHub, Jira, and employee calendar activity. All API fetching,
              parsing, context truncation, and inference occur on the local client machine.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">06 · Privacy Strategy</span>
            <p>
              LogPulse is designed for zero remote data transmission. Raw employee
              activity never leaves the client machine, preserving privacy while enabling
              offline-friendly summarization.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">07 · Model Evaluation</span>
            <p>
              Minimum viable performance requires at least 95% fact-recall precision,
              less than 1% hallucinated facts, strict zero fabrication, end-to-end latency
              under 5 seconds, and low or no operating cost.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">08 · Fallback UX</span>
            <p>
              Timeout state: "Request timed out." Low confidence state: "Model returned
              an unexpected output format. Displaying formatted raw activity log below."
              API failure state: "Failed to fetch."
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>


<style>
.prd {
  padding: 120px 0 80px;
}

.prd-intro {
  color:var(--text-secondary);
  max-width:760px;
  font-size:1.05rem;
  margin-bottom:28px;
}

.prd-meta {
  display:flex;
  flex-wrap:wrap;
  gap:12px;
  margin-bottom:40px;
}

.prd-meta span {
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  color:var(--text-secondary);
  padding:8px 14px;
  border-radius:999px;
  font-size:0.9rem;
}

.prd-spec {
  border-top:1px solid var(--border);
}

.prd-spec-row {
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:280px 1fr;
  gap:40px;
  padding:26px 0;
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
}

.prd-spec-label {
  color:var(--accent);
  font-weight:700;
  font-size:0.95rem;
  letter-spacing:0.02em;
}

.prd-spec-row p {
  color:var(--text-secondary);
  max-width:640px;
}

@media(max-width:800px){

  .prd {
    padding:100px 0 60px;
  }

  .prd-spec-row{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
    gap:10px;
  }

}

@media(max-width:480px){

  .prd {
    padding:90px 0 60px;
  }

}
</style>
